{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the unfinished thread-index cleanup from retired #2915 and finding 5 of the later round-two review. Queue after your existing work through #21350; keep #21351 in its already-agreed earlier position. Do not interrupt active implementations, reviews or full Tailapp I7.\n\nThe old rendering components were removed, but the [current thread index](ui/src/lib/threads.ts@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:48) still builds an unused summary map and copies its growing child list on every insertion. The [barrel exports](ui/src/lib/store.ts@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:5) retain threadChildren and ThreadSummary without production consumers. The [graph](ui/src/lib/outcomeMap.ts@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:160) now needs roots and cycle diagnostics, while the [spine](ui/src/lib/spine.ts@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:109) needs content. Preserve those newer consumers; the historical proposal to treat content as the sole consumer is obsolete.\n\n[Measured work](thread-copy-evidence.json): at 1,000, 2,000 and 4,000 direct replies the actual child-list spread yields 499,500, 1,999,000 and 7,998,000 existing entries. The read-only [reproduction](thread-copy-replay.py) instruments a temporary copy of the exact current source and compares roots, root content, root summary and cycles with the unmodified implementation. This demonstrates quadratic adjacency construction on these star-shaped inputs, not browser latency or the complexity of every graph operation. Display limits do not bound this work: buildOutcomeMap constructs the full index first. [Current basis reconciliation](thread-current-bases.json) verifies the live cited source revisions are incorporated in main and byte-identical at the examined paths.\n\nDeliver one bounded UI repair:\n1. Recheck current imports/callers. Remove only unused thread summary computation/types and the threadChildren wrapper/barrel exports, plus tests that solely protect those removed APIs. Preserve useful root/content/cycle and navigation tests.\n2. Build each parent's child list with work proportional to its edges, preserving insertion order and all existing thread semantics. No arbitrary input truncation, changed parent selection, hidden cycles, removed commitment boundaries or weakened graph warnings. Keep returned content and deterministic root ordering unchanged, including missing parents and malformed cycles.\n3. Add small deterministic behavior and actual-work regressions. Cover empty input, wide fan-out, a deep chain, multiple commitments, missing bases and cycles. Demonstrate that restoring the repeated-copy operation fails the work check while semantic controls still pass. Count actual operations or allocations within the construction; no elapsed-time pass threshold or self-reported constant counter. State the bounded cost proved without claiming the entire graph is linear.\n4. Verify actual Thread and OutcomeMap consumers with existing UI tests and a browser smoke check on small and large histories. Run npm test --prefix ui, TypeScript/build and make ui-check with the regenerated committed embed; run the appropriate repository/documentation checks. Publish exact-path artifacts, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratify the verdict, seal main delivery, push, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch.\n\nUse request/thread-index-cleanup from then-current main. This preserves the layer 7 presentation contract; update architecture documentation only if the implementation changes that contract. No server /v0/graph or /v0/worktrees contract, durable workflow, signing path, global cache or unrelated UI redesign belongs here. The original TopBar/per-component derivation consolidation and other dead client APIs remain separately identified residual opportunities; this task does not claim all of #2915 complete. Ordinary source staleness is acknowledged; the exact current bytes, required behavior and authorization for this recovery have been reconciled.\n","body":{"branch":"request/thread-index-cleanup","conditions":"Remove unused thread-summary/wrapper work and quadratic child-list copying while preserving current roots/content/cycles, graph warnings, commitment boundaries and ordering; prove actual work and behavior, independently review and complete sealed/pushed/green main delivery with cleanup.","head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0bbb2ebe1ce87fc892a82a0f99a419cd37e1b052, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:62aa89bdf256cc50d4cf87ad12841c820dc2597c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fd8c0359b661ccffd88b5496b4652c40e9aa398e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00111141fa306515e5cd544b834349e87f9d22cf, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b8a9ff517318daec88e265b848e08ea877e98fa and 55 more","target_head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}